cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ViSPACE in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ViSPACE: Virchow2 powered Spatial Characterization and feature Extraction Pipeline"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Srivastava
    given-names: Himangi
    email: himangisrivastava45@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/himangi2003/ViSPACE"
abstract: >-
  ViSPACE is an end-to-end computational pathology pipeline for analysing
  whole-slide images in lung and breast cancer. It combines the Virchow2
  foundation model with a pixel-wise segmentation decoder to produce
  five-class tissue segmentations and extract quantitative spatial
  biomarkers from the tumor microenvironment.
keywords:
  - computational pathology
  - digital pathology
  - whole-slide imaging
  - tumor microenvironment
  - segmentation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Virchow2: Scaling Self-Supervised Mixed Magnification Models in Pathology"
    authors:
